<h2>A "move," a "rung," a "delegation"</h2>
<p>A <strong>move</strong> is a planned step in the project's roadmap (Move 1, Move 2 …) — an internal sequence, not a game. A <strong>rung</strong> is a level on the project's evidence ladder, from "fact" up to "theory"; to say "no rung has moved" is to say no claim has gained or lost evidential standing. A <strong>standing delegation</strong> is a stretch where the author asked the machine to keep working autonomously; each was <a href="{{ '/standing/' | url }}">booked as a cost and left provisional</a> until his review — which came at Session 4k, when he ruled on them item-by-item and closed the build.</p>

<p class="companion-note">If a term on this site still reads as jargon after this page, that is a finding, not your failure — and it is on the record as one.</p>
